      <div type="clause" n="11.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ExcomI">Excom I</ref> 11.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Excom I 11.2" corresp="#wit-ti"><pb n="433" ed="#liebermann"/>a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.24"/> pretiosi corporis et sanguinis Domini perceptione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="i" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.i"/> et a societate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="k" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.k"/> omnium Christianorum separamus et a liminibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.l"/> sanctę matris æcclesiæ in cęlo et in terra excludimus et excommunicatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.25"/> et anathematizatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.25"/> esse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.26"/> decernimus et dampnatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.25"/> cum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="m" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.m"/> diabolo et angelis eius et omnibus reprobis in igne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="n" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.n"/> æterno iudicamus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.star"/>,</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann"/>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Matth. 25, 41</note>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 433 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">433</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Am Rande, vom Textschreiber, Ti (fehlt übrigen):</hi> [11, 3] <hi rend="spaced">Interrogatio</hi>{1}: Excommunicatis et uos? <hi rend="spaced">Responsio</hi>: Excommunicamus. [11, 4] <hi rend="spaced">Interrogatio</hi>: Dampnatis et uos? [<hi rend="spaced">Responsio</hi>{2}:] Dampnamus. [11, 5] Excommunicati et d[amp]nati{2} et maledicti sint; et sicut{3} extinguntur candelę istę, sic e[xtin]guantur{2} animę illorum in{4} infe[rno{2}].</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">In the margin, by the scribe of the text, Ti (missing in the others):</hi> [11, 3] <hi rend="italic">Interrogatio</hi>{1}: Excommunicatis et uos? <hi rend="italic">Responsio</hi>: Excommunicamus. [11, 4] <hi rend="italic">Interrogatio</hi>: Dampnatis et uos? [<hi rend="italic">Responsio</hi>{2}:] Dampnamus. [11, 5] Excommunicati et d[amp]nati{2} et maledicti sint; et sicut{3} extinguntur candelę istę, sic e[xtin]guantur{2} animę illorum in{4} infe[rno{2}].</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ExcomI_11-2.lnote.oe.i" n="i" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">433</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> II 4. <hi rend="italic">Rem Sen Urg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> II 4. <hi rend="italic">Rem Sen Urg</hi></seg></note>
